<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Wet fields halt harvest.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Wet fields halt harvest.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soggy fields halted harvest activities in Texas and Oklahoma Wednesday, but grain merchandisers said they expected dry weather conditions would allow cutting to resume and be in full swing by the weekend.</p>
<p>&quot;Some areas received anywhere between a sprinkle to 3-1/2 inches of rain Monday into yesterday,&quot; an Oklahoma dealer said. &quot;Today it's cool and there's no wind, so (the fields) are drying out real slowly.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;If it doesn't rain today, it'll continue to get to the point where we can cut again by the weekend,&quot; another Oklahoma dealer said.</p>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were mostly steady to weaker Wednesday.</p>
